<title>USA: Tracor unit gets $15.5 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Tracor unit gets $15.5 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>GDE Systems Inc, a San Diego- based unit of Tracor Inc, said it received an 18-month, $15.5 million contract to develop and deliver three, deployable Tactical Exploitation Group (TEG) ground station systems to the U.S. Marine Corps.</p>
<p>The TEG, which provides real-time exploitation of reconnaissance imagery from the F-18 imaging system, is the first product delivery order issued under the Reconnaissance/Intelligence Ground Systems Products and Services (RPS) umbrella contract.</p>
</text>
